# Third-party includes

Vendored and external library headers use **angle brackets**. Quotes are for **project** headers only (paths from the library subfolder, never `Core/` or the repo root).

This includes the standalone products under `ThirdParty/` — **Logging**, **Parallel**, and **Profiler** — as well as fmt, gtest, benchmark, and the rest.

```cpp
// BAD — third-party with quotes
#include "fmt/format.h"
#include "gtest/gtest.h"
#include "logger/logger.h"
#include "native/session/profiler.h"
#include "tools/threaded_callback_queue.h"

// GOOD — third-party with <>
#include <fmt/format.h>
#include <gtest/gtest.h>
#include <logger/logger.h>
#include <native/session/profiler.h>
#include <bespoke/kineto/profiler_kineto.h>
#include <tools/threaded_callback_queue.h>
#include <util/exception.h>

// GOOD — project headers stay quoted
#include "common/macros.h"
#include "memory/helper/memory_allocator.h"
#include "profiler/gpu_memory_snapshot.h"
```

Do not write `#include "third_party/..."`. Use the installed/public header, e.g. `#include <fmt/format.h>`.
Never edit files under `ThirdParty/` to satisfy this; fix the include site instead.

Do **not** treat `"profiler/"` as Profiler. That prefix is first-party `Library/Memory/profiler/`. Profiler public headers are `<native/...>` and `<bespoke/...>`. Do **not** treat generic `"util/"` or `"tools/"` as third-party — only Logging's `<util/exception.h>` and Parallel's `<tools/threaded_callback_queue.h>`.
